FILEMGR resource-archive lookup FUN_0000_5d50 (extender op-0x18 MAP-LOAD, palette 532.pal from the
XOR-encoded PAL.RES archive): pass the ORIGINAL member-name pointer to FUN_0000_6250, not the
__allregs-garbage param_3.  When the direct findfirst on a member name fails and a resource dir
(PTR_s_RESOURCE_RES_0000_622c = "PAL.RES") is set, 5d50 calls 6250 (the archive-member opener) which
reads the name char-by-char via `lodsb` from ESI.  In the asm ESI is the incoming name pointer, SAVED at
entry (5d51 `push esi`) and RESTORED just before the call (5df6 `pop esi`) because the uppercase-copy
loop consumes it.  Ghidra dropped that save/restore and, worse, threaded 6250's ESI param as 5cc2's
uVar1 = CONCAT22(extraout_var, R_DX) -- a bogus 0x4e00b480 -> 6250's `*param_2` wild-dereferenced ->
SIGSEGV.  Fix: capture param_6 (the incoming name = TCB+0x9a "532.pal") at entry and pass it to 6250.
This path was never exercised before (KDV's TITLE.KDV is a standalone file found by the first findfirst,
so 5d50's resource-archive branch never ran).
